      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "YONDU BALE (2) has a strong winning strike-rate here having won two of three starts. Comes off a (25.57) win last time, scoring by 1.1 lengths in a Grade 5 over 450m at Ballarat. Expected to be in the finish. PADDY'S WAY (3) was big odds last time but gave a huge sight after a fast early split and ran away with a 1.5 lengths win at this track over 450m in 25.74. Can make it back-to-back wins. MARCO MARCO (1) hit the ground running off the low draw last start and was never headed (22.23) at Ballarat in a Grade 5 over 390m. Boasts two wins from two starts out of this box. Can make it back-to-back wins. CACKLING SUZIE (7) is a last-start placegetter and ran good time - in the mix again.",
